Suggested-by: Greg Kroah-Hartman <gregkh@linuxfoundation.org>
Signed-off-by: Jimmy Hu <hhhuuu@google.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260320065427.1374555-1-hhhuuu@google.com
Signed-off-by: Greg Kroah-Hartman <gregkh@linuxfoundation.org>

Here is the root cause:
The bug is a race condition in `uvc_function_unbind()` where it nullifies the gadget pointer (`cdev->gadget = NULL`) after wait events abort early due to PM freeze. A concurrent V4L2 release (`uvc_v4l2_release`) then calls `uvc_function_disconnect()` → `usb_function_deactivate()` → `usb_gadget_deactivate()`, which dereferences the now-NULL gadget pointer, causing a kernel panic. The timing-based wait (`wait_event_interruptible_timeout`) is insufficient during PM transitions because freezing user-space processes can wake the wait prematurely, allowing unbind to proceed before the application releases the video device.

